/server.ts` `/api/actions.json` does `if (state) list = list.filter((a) => a.state === state);`. Valid action states are `new | applied | rejected | superseded` (`src/actions.ts:228`), so `state=all` matches nothing and returns `[]`. `state=new` works, which matches the report.\n- **Fix scope (small, one file plus a test):** treat `state=all` as no state filter, e.g. `if (state && state !== \"all\")`, and document it in the README next to the `state=new` contract. Add a regression test in `pm-stack/aggregator/test/actions.test.ts` that stores applied actions and asserts `?state=all` returns them. `?state=new` stays unchanged.\n- **Blockers and ordering:** none. The fix is independent and can run as a small-fix task. It should land before the weekly triage retrospective (code#1455) relies on the API again.\n- **Links:** #4620 · code#1455 · queue task 8431\n<!-- agent-note:v1 agent=repo-worker-code lane=c29174f1-48e0-4b13-b4ff-9b73ab67e9ab state=triaged at=2026-11-03T19:48Z -->","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/comments/6613835307/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/comments/6613928574","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/4620#issuecomment-6613928574","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/4620","id":6613928574,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJWP4788AAAABijiKfg","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"h